{"id": "1549892369892245518", "channel_id": "1543844957859745862", "author_id": "693905974750216212", "author_name": "fishhazardthewizard", "content": "Even her current critical damage scaling provides rapid diminishing returns, because her base damage numbers are EXTREMELY low, especially in the modern standards of the game. A single 280-300 damage hit, even multiplied by 400% simply isn’t even remotely enough to progress steadily through the normal story, let alone in endgame levels such as Phantasmal Dive or the DZone. \nIf you’re wondering where the 280-300 number comes from, I did an extensive calculation table on various wheel equipment for Jenkins, found here: https://discord.com/channels/1131791637933199470/1170692781216378960/1541343906921451520\nAt the time of the data collection, I had a lv90 Jenkin at +12, with all “Gnostic Potential” levels unlocked. \n\nJenkin is one of the first characters that players meet in the main story, and she’s one of the most unforgettable ones, first as the companion to Aigis, and then as our savior in the Wax Museum. With the game’s core concept of fighting against forgetting, shouldn’t you be caring more about characters like her?", "timestamp": "2026-09-16T21:18:56.590000+00:00", "type": 19, "thread_id": "1543844957859745862", "reactions": [{"emoji": "🧡", "emoji_id": null, "count": 2}, {"emoji": "Celeste_agree", "emoji_id": "1400771815076528258", "count": 1}, {"emoji": "🔥", "emoji_id": null, "count": 2}], "reply_to": "1546762640821329940", "thread_title": "Do not Forget: Jenkins", "forum_channel_id": "1180845276823564288", "thread_tags": ["1542484945447026708", "1542484013652910141"]}
{"id": "1549892736004395091", "channel_id": "1543844957859745862", "author_id": "693905974750216212", "author_name": "fishhazardthewizard", "content": "Do not Forget: Jenkins", "timestamp": "2026-09-16T21:20:23.878000+00:00", "type": 4, "thread_id": "1543844957859745862", "thread_title": "Do not Forget: Jenkins", "forum_channel_id": "1180845276823564288", "thread_tags": ["1542484945447026708", "1542484013652910141"]}
{"id": "1549906133584715877", "channel_id": "1543844957859745862", "author_id": "310254141639491590", "author_name": "alexisvaunt", "content": "I feel like the best way to fix it without resorting to %HP would be to change the damage increase from flat %ATK to %-current-damage, or have it increase base damage by a % of base damage. So that as you keep using the attack, it scales faster and faster. It would still be comparatively slow, and would be balanced for both high level and low level content by default. But depending on how you play, that sort of (low-)exponential growth could be as effective as 24's scaling, I think? Or I'm talking out my ass lol. But like, increases base damage by 5% or 10% of current (/current base, but that would probably need higher scaling to work?) damage would feel a lot better to me, at least.", "timestamp": "2026-09-16T22:13:38.110000+00:00", "thread_id": "1543844957859745862", "thread_title": "Do not Forget: Jenkins", "forum_channel_id": "1180845276823564288", "thread_tags": ["1542484945447026708", "1542484013652910141"]}
